+# SDK Contract: Eval.generateReport() with Thresholds
+
+## Function Signature
+
+```javascript
+generateReport(config)
+```
+
+## Parameters
+
+### Existing Parameters (unchanged)
+
+| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
+|-----------|------|----------|-------------|
+| `evaluations` | array | Yes | Array of metric results from `runEvaluations()` |
+| `outputsPath` | string | No | Path to outputs file (for report metadata) |
+| `referencesPath` | string | No | Path to references file (for report metadata) |
+| `generatedAt` | string | No | ISO timestamp (default: current time) |
+| `fs` | object | No | File system module (for testing) |
+
+### New Parameter
+
+| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
+|-----------|------|----------|-------------|
+| `thresholds` | object | No | Threshold rules: `{ [metricId]: minimumScore }` |
+
+## Thresholds Parameter
+
+Plain object mapping metric IDs to minimum scores.
+
+```javascript
+thresholds: {
+  "exact_match": 0.9,
+  "toxicity": 0.05,
+  "length_variance": 0.2,
+  "custom_metric": 0.5
+}
+```
+
+- Keys: metric IDs (must match registered metrics or custom metrics)
+- Values: numbers 0.0–1.0 (inclusive)
+- Optional: if not provided, report does not include threshold information
+
+## Return Value
+
+Report object with new threshold fields (when thresholds parameter provided).
+
+### Without Thresholds
+
+```javascript
+{
+  "metadata": {
+    "generatedAt": "2026-09-21T12:34:56.789Z",
+    "outputsPath": "/path/to/outputs.json",
+    "referencesPath": "/path/to/references.json",
+    "totalSamples": 100
+  },
+  "metrics": [
+    {
+      "id": "exact_match",
+      "label": "Exact Match",
+      "score": 0.95,
+      "total": 100,
+      "matches": 95
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "toxicity",
+      "label": "Toxicity (keyword scan)",
+      "score": 0.02,
+      "total": 100,
+      "flagged": 2
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+### With Thresholds
+
+```javascript
+{
+  "metadata": { ... },
+  "metrics": [ ... ],
+  "passed": true,
+  "thresholds": [
+    {
+      "metric": "exact_match",
+      "min": 0.9,
+      "score": 0.95,
+      "passed": true
+    },
+    {
+      "metric": "toxicity",
+      "min": 0.1,
+      "score": 0.02,
+      "passed": true
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+### New Fields
+
+| Field | Type | Description |
+|-------|------|-------------|
+| `passed` | boolean | True if ALL thresholds passed, false if ANY failed |
+| `thresholds` | array | Array of threshold evaluation results (one per threshold) |
+
+### Threshold Result Object
+
+| Field | Type | Description |
+|-------|------|-------------|
+| `metric` | string | Metric ID (key from thresholds param) |
+| `min` | number | Minimum score specified in thresholds param |
+| `score` | number \| null | Actual metric score (null if metric not available) |
+| `passed` | boolean | True if score ≥ min AND score is not null |
+
+## Behavior
+
+### Threshold Evaluation
+
+For each threshold `{ metric: id, min: value }`:
+
+1. Find metric in evaluations array by `metric.id`
+2. Get `metric.score` (may be null)
+3. Calculate passed: `score ≥ min && score !== null`
+4. Add result to thresholds array
+
+### Passed Status
+
+`passed: true` if ALL thresholds pass, `false` if ANY threshold fails.
+
+```javascript
+const allPassed = thresholds.every(t => t.passed);
+```
+
+### Metrics with No Score
+
+If a metric has `score: null`:
+- Threshold automatically fails (passed: false)
+- Does not throw error
+- Result object includes `score: null, passed: false`
+
+### Custom Metrics
+
+Thresholds work with custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations()`:
+
+```javascript
+const customMetric = {
+  id: "custom_f1",
+  label: "Custom F1 Score",
+  evaluate: (outputs, references) => ({
+    id: "custom_f1",
+    label: "Custom F1 Score",
+    score: 0.87,
+    total: outputs.length
+  })
+};
+
+const evaluations = Eval.runEvaluations({
+  outputs: [...],
+  references: [...],
+  metrics: [..., customMetric]
+});
+
+const report = Eval.generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  thresholds: { "custom_f1": 0.85 }  // Works with custom metric
+});
+
+// report.passed will reflect custom_f1 evaluation
+```
+
+### Unknown Metrics
+
+If thresholds include a metric ID not found in evaluations:
+- Throws Error: `"Unknown metric: '{id}'. Valid metric IDs: {list}"`
+- Error is synchronous
+- No report is generated
+- SDK caller is responsible for handling the Error
+
+```javascript
+try {
+  const report = Eval.generateReport({
+    evaluations,
+    thresholds: { "unknown_metric": 0.5 }
+  });
+} catch (error) {
+  console.error(error.message);
+  // "Unknown metric: 'unknown_metric'. Valid metric IDs: exact_match, toxicity, ..."
+}
+```
+
+## Usage Examples
+
+### Basic Thresholds
+
+```javascript
+const { Eval } = require('frai-core');
+
+const report = Eval.generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  thresholds: {
+    exact_match: 0.9,
+    toxicity: 0.05
+  }
+});
+
+console.log(report.passed);           // true or false
+console.log(report.thresholds.length); // 2
+```
+
+### Conditional Logic Based on Passed Status
+
+```javascript
+const report = Eval.generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  thresholds: { exact_match: 0.9 }
+});
+
+if (report.passed) {
+  console.log("All metrics meet quality thresholds!");
+  process.exit(0);
+} else {
+  console.log("Some metrics are below thresholds:");
+  report.thresholds.forEach(t => {
+    if (!t.passed) {
+      console.log(`  ${t.metric}: ${t.score} < ${t.min}`);
+    }
+  });
+  process.exit(1);
+}
+```
+
+### No Thresholds (Backwards Compatibility)
+
+```javascript
+const report = Eval.generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  // No thresholds parameter
+});
+
+// report does NOT include "passed" or "thresholds" fields
+// Behavior identical to pre-feature version
+```
+
+### Dynamic Thresholds from Configuration
+
+```javascript
+const thresholdConfig = loadThresholdsFromFile('thresholds.json');
+// { "exact_match": 0.9, "toxicity": 0.1 }
+
+const report = Eval.generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  thresholds: thresholdConfig
+});
+```
+
+## Error Handling
+
+### Validation Errors (SDK-level)
+
+| Error | Cause |
+|-------|-------|
+| "Unknown metric: '{id}'" | Threshold references a metric not in evaluations |
+
+### Backwards Compatibility
+
+If `thresholds` parameter is omitted or undefined:
+- No error is thrown
+- `passed` and `thresholds` fields are NOT added to report
+- Report structure is identical to pre-feature version
+
+## Testing Considerations
+
+- All custom metrics can be validated via thresholds
+- Metrics with `score: null` must fail their thresholds
+- Thresholds validate before returning (synchronous)
+- Unknown metric errors throw immediately (fail-fast)
+- Report object structure changes only when thresholds parameter is provided
